    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_MenuStep5">Card Modes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_StepIndicatorFormat">STEP {0} OF {1}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step1Desc">Each player holds cards based on the chosen mode. The dangerous ones are called Fatal Meow Cats. The rest are safe — choose wisely what you play and what you hide.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatEgyptian">Egyptian Cat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatEgyptianSub">Safe · Ancient Power</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatZombie">Zombie Cat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatZombieSub">Safe · Undying Spirit</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatGuardian">Guardian Cat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatGuardianSub">Safe · Dark Protector</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatFatal">Fatal Meow Cat</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CatFatalSub">Dangerous</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CardsPerPlayer">CARDS PER PLAYER</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step2Desc">On your turn, you place exactly ONE card face-down in front of you — or you may pass and open a bid instead. Cards cannot be revealed until challenged. Bluffing is encouraged!</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step2Action">Place exactly ONE card face-down — or pass to open a bid:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step3Desc">After placing cards, players bid on how many safe cards they can flip across ALL players' stacks — starting with their own. Each bid must be higher than the last. You may pass instead of bidding.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_BidExample">Bid example:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_CurrentBid">← Current bid: 7</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step4Desc">The highest bidder flips exactly that many cards, starting from their own pile. Each successfully completed challenge scores a point. If you hit a Fatal Meow Cat, you choose which card to discard permanently.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_FlippingOrder">Flipping order — start from your own pile:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_YouFirst">You (first)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_OpponentA">Opponent A</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_OpponentB">Opponent B</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_ChallengesToWin">CHALLENGES TO WIN</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_SuccessfulChallenges">successful challenges</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_Step5Desc">Choose how many cards each player holds before the match. More cards mean more bluffing — and in 8-card mode, two Fatal Meow Cats per player unlock The Fugitive Kitten bonus before the match begins.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_ModesAtGlance">MODES AT A GLANCE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_8CardOnly">8-CARD MODE ONLY</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_FugitiveKitten">The Fugitive Kitten</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_FugitiveKittenDesc">appears before each match. The first player to catch it earns 1 extra life.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_ExtraLife">Extra life:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="HowToPlay_ExtraLifeDesc">your first Fatal Meow Cat doesn't fail the challenge — the reveal continues; you only fail on the second.</sys:String>
